    {
      "number": 59,
      "source_text_sha256": "80d4f5d831c758e3d5ea7fc29d896330f6ff09764acaed40833b0ee63799360a",
      "lines": [
        "Background: KV Caching (for Attention)",
        "https://medium.com/@joaolages/kv-caching-explained-276520203249",
        "Only applies to generative (autoregressive) models",
        "(Operations repeated in",
        "future time steps have",
        "results stored in cache)",
        "Limitations: uses memory",
        "inefficiently since needed",
        "cache size regularly changes",
        "and reserves lots of cache",
        "memory to support large sizes",
        "Store Keys and Values"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 60,
      "source_text_sha256": "0c25dada3de1f6aa8ad9ca158694177c157aa6512a648007f1fbbf08d1b58dbe",
      "lines": [
        "V3/R1 Solution: Multi-Head Latent Attention",
        "DeepSeek-V3 paper. 2024",
        "Architecturally, adds a small number",
        "of parameters to project KV cache to",
        "a smaller vector; only this vector must",
        "be cached at inference"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 61,
      "source_text_sha256": "3922c8493e549c135cb58ee47764b691b39ca722f148f4a7e37f66bebbee1599",
      "lines": [
        "Also Relevant: vLLM Offers an Inference Trick",
        "Kwon et al. Efficient Memory Management for Large Language Model Serving with PagedAttention. SOSP 2023",
        "• Inspiration: virtual memory with paging used in operating systems to limit memory fragmentation",
        "by allocating memory “pages” on demand",
        "• Idea: an LLM serving engine using PageAttention, which allocates KV cache into fixed-size blocks",
        "(aka, “pages”) that don’t have to be contiguous"
      ]
    },
